IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Income Tax Act 1947 (Singapore) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- A fact here is one a witness or a document could give ("she spent 190 days
-- in Singapore in 2024"); whether that makes her "resident in Singapore" is a
-- rule.
--
-- Source: ../source/ITA1947.txt (SSO PDF, current version as at 06 Oct 2026).

§ `Income Tax Act 1947 — the nouns`

§§ `Persons (s 2, Parts 11 and 15)`

-- s 2 "person" includes a company, a body of persons and a Hindu joint family;
-- s 42(1) and s 43(1) sort persons for the rate of tax.
DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company`
    `a body of persons`
    `a Hindu joint family`
    `a trustee of an incapacitated person`
    `a trustee of another trust`
    `an executor`

-- s 2 "resident in Singapore", (a) individuals: the facts of the year
-- preceding the year of assessment.
DECLARE `Residence facts` HAS
    `resides in Singapore, except reasonable temporary absences` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a), first limb: a finding
    `days physically present in Singapore`                        IS A NUMBER    -- (a), second limb; s 2(2): part of a day counts as a day
    `days exercising an employment in Singapore, other than as a director` IS A NUMBER
    `control and management of the business exercised in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN -- (b) companies and bodies of persons

§§ `Income (s 10)`

-- s 10(1): the heads of income charged.
DECLARE `Head of income` IS ONE OF
    `(a) gains or profits from a trade, business, profession or vocation`
    `(b) gains or profits from employment`
    `(d) dividends, interest or discounts`
    `(e) a pension, charge or annuity`
    `(f) rents, royalties, premiums and other profits from property`
    `(g) other gains or profits of an income nature`

-- s 10(1), s 12: where the income is from.
DECLARE `Source of income` IS ONE OF
    `accruing in or derived from Singapore`
    `received in Singapore from outside Singapore`
    `outside Singapore and not received in Singapore`

§§ `Years of assessment`

-- s 2 "year of assessment": the 12 months from 1 January; YAs are numbered by
-- the calendar year. The basis period is, for most income, the preceding
-- calendar year (s 35).
DECLARE `Year of assessment` HAS
    `year` IS A NUMBER
